# Authority: what a user may do, and how far it reaches.
#
# A role is a name for a set of authorities. An authority is a **kind** at a
# **reach** — `read`, `write`, `manage`, `govern` or `operate`, over the store,
# over one namespace, or over one database. Nothing is implied by anything else
# except containment down the tenancy, and that one-way implication is the whole
# model: holding `write` over a namespace does not confer `manage` over it, so
# writing records where databases live does not confer creating or dropping
# them.
#
# The reach is keyword-led in every spelling — `STORE`, `NAMESPACE x`,
# `DATABASE x.y` — so that a table can never be read as a reach. `STORE` is a
# reserved word for exactly that reason: `GRANT read ON store TO ada` is a
# statement that already meant the *table* `store`, and a reach spelled as a
# bare word would have silently widened it.
#
# A corpus file is one anonymous session, the same as `grants.tessariql`, so
# what these cases pin is the shape of the statements and the refusals reachable
# before the first `DEFINE USER` closes the store. What an authority *does* to a
# signed-in session is asserted in `crates/tessari-session/tests/authorities.rs`,
# where a session can sign in.

--- case: two namespaces and a database, to reach at
DEFINE NAMESPACE prod;
USE NAMESPACE prod;
DEFINE DATABASE shop;
USE DATABASE shop;
DEFINE TABLE orders;
--- expect: ok

--- case: a second namespace, so that a reach can be wrong rather than absent
DEFINE NAMESPACE staging;
--- expect: ok

--- case: an authority names a kind this store has
GRANT scribble ON STORE TO nobody;
--- expect: error NoSuchAuthority

--- case: and so does a revocation
REVOKE scribble ON NAMESPACE prod FROM nobody;
--- expect: error NoSuchAuthority

--- case: a reach names a namespace that exists
GRANT manage ON NAMESPACE nonesuch TO nobody;
--- expect: error Unknown

--- case: a reach names a database that exists
GRANT manage ON DATABASE prod.nonesuch TO nobody;
--- expect: error Unknown

--- case: an authority names a user, and there is none yet
GRANT manage ON NAMESPACE prod TO nobody;
--- expect: error Unknown

--- case: a role is one spelling of a set, and it still works
DEFINE USER ada ON prod.shop ROLE editor PASSWORD 'correct horse';
--- expect: ok

--- case: handing out authority is administering, so an anonymous session may not
GRANT manage ON NAMESPACE prod TO ada;
--- expect: error NotSignedIn

--- case: and neither may it take one back
REVOKE manage ON NAMESPACE prod FROM ada;
--- expect: error NotSignedIn

--- case: the set is the other spelling, and declaring one is administering too
DEFINE USER nadia ON NAMESPACE prod AUTHORITIES manage PASSWORD 'x';
--- expect: error NotSignedIn

--- case: reading who holds what is reading the permission system
INFO FOR USER ada;
--- expect: error NotSignedIn

--- case: a table may no longer be named `store`, which is what reserving it cost
DEFINE TABLE store;
--- expect: error UnexpectedToken
